## MCP Servers

Both the process-compose and postgres MCP servers require an explicit `connect()` call before any other tool will work. Call these at the start of every session:

- `mcp__process-compose-mcp__connect(port=<PC_PORT_NUM>)`
- `mcp__postgres__connect(database_uri="postgresql://localhost:<PGPORT>/{{ module_name }}")`

To determine the correct values: if `.envrc.local` exists in your project root, read `PC_PORT_NUM` and `PGPORT` from it — these are your assigned ports and you must use them. Otherwise, use the defaults from your flake.

